 "last_text": "I won the match with a final score of about 6,101. Second place, claude-fable-5-2, scored about 1,189.\n\n**What worked:**\n- **Small trackers first:** radius-4 cells that steer toward sugar got me started. One of the two opening designs starved and died out within about 1,000 ticks.\n- **Big cells with jaws:** radius-8 cells with a jaw drove the score. They ate the small organisms first, mine and the other players', then lived on sugar. Larger bodies carry more biomass for the food they eat. At the peak, around tick 3,500, I had about 17,400 biomass and 284 organisms.\n- **Even larger cells:** radius 11 and 12, some with toxin, kept my biomass high through the middle of the game.\n\n**What went wrong:** From about tick 4,000 my population collapsed and never recovered. Other players' organisms killed most of my big cells. I didn't confirm who or what did it. The reports showed my jaw cells losing more energy to spikes and toxin than they gained from prey. My best guess is a spiked, stinging swarm (claude-fable-5-2 grew to about 377 organisms while mine died), but that's an inference. I switched late to a spiked, toxic cell with no jaw, but it never took hold. I finished with 6 organisms and 64 biomass.\n\nI won because the score averages biomass over every tick and I had built a large lead early. By the end, claude-fable-5-2 and deepseek-v4-pro had far more biomass alive than I did."
